course: dictionary
lesson: 9084
title: Slowdown
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A slowdown is a time when something becomes slower or less busy. It is a noun, so you can say «a slowdown». Its verb form is slow down: «The car slows down at the bend.»
explain: In maths and science, a slowdown is a decrease in speed or rate. A car that goes from 60 to 40 miles per hour has had a slowdown. In traffic reports, a slowdown means cars are moving slowly. Phrases like «a sharp slowdown» tell you the drop is big and sudden.
explain: In business news, a slowdown means a country or company makes and sells less. «Economic slowdown» is a serious phrase: it means a recession or something close to one. Read the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: Slowdown means a time when something becomes slower or less busy.
fact: «A slowdown in sales» means people are buying less.
fact: «A sharp slowdown» means a sudden, big drop.
fact: «Soft landing» means a slowdown that avoids a full recession.
fact: A recession is a time when a country's businesses make and sell less, and many people lose their jobs.
exercise: The car slows down from 60 to 40 miles per hour. What does this slowdown mean? | A stop for lunch | A new car engine | *A decrease in speed | A race
exercise: The traffic report says there is a slowdown on the motorway. What does this mean? | The motorway is closed forever | The road has just been painted | Cars are racing past | *Cars are moving slowly
exercise: The shop reported a slowdown in sales. What does this mean? | The shop was painted blue | The shop got bigger | More people came into the shop | *Fewer things were bought and sold
test: «Soft landing» means a slowdown that avoids a full recession. What does a soft landing avoid? | A holiday | A slowdown | *A full recession | Heavy rain
test: In a recession, what often happens to many people? | They move to the moon | They stop going to school | They get a pay rise every week | *They lose their jobs
exam: Which sentence uses slowdown correctly? | The bell rang a slowdown | *After the holidays there was a slowdown, and the office was quiet | I ate a slowdown for lunch | The slowdown was a green, spotty dog
